\section*{Single-letter classical capacity of generalized amplitude damping}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Every generalized amplitude-damping qubit channel is claimed to have an explicit one-variable unassisted capacity formula achieved by binary pure states, with the listed universal partner-channel additivities.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
A block-entropy inequality is reduced to log-determinant comparisons and contraction convexity. This controls correlated channel inputs, proves the one-use binary optimum, and extends the entropy and Holevo bounds to arbitrary finite-dimensional tensor partners.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Every generalized amplitude-damping qubit channel is claimed to have an explicit one-variable unassisted capacity formula achieved by binary pure states, with the listed universal partner-channel additivities. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 276, the documented theorem gives the attained scalar capacity formula and repeated-use additivity for the same amplitude-damping channel. Additivity with arbitrary different partner channels is beyond this entry. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{AmplitudeDamping.lean}. Named declarations include \texttt{OAI.GAD.main}. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

